A||N||5||WhiteFieroBlur||Getting a loan for a kit||||1||
Z||000000||WhiteFieroBlur||11-04-2001||04:22 AM||||I have a loan for my fiero for a few thousands and it should be paid for soon by my bank. I was wondering if anyone ever thought about taking out a loan to buy a kit. Since I won't have a car payment anymore I was wondering about buying a lambo kit or some kit.<P> How much average would like a lamborgini kit cost all together. And do you think they would give me a loan for this?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||11-04-2001||06:34 AM||||Its a llittle tricky getting loan for a kit. They like having a finished product that they can touch. It can be done though. May need a lot of documentation to show them as to the value when its done, your abilities to be able to do it. I just talked to my bank about buying a kit. Ive been with them for like 20 years and the manager told me basicly since they know im in that business and know Id actually finish it there would be no problem and they would put no reasonable limits to the loan. They did however say the maximum they would carry the note was 48 months. I was figuring about $22,000 making the payments around $595 @ month.<P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1234884&a=11878523&p=52990885"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||11-04-2001||07:15 AM||||I would expect that you would have difficulty for a loan on the kit.  However an unsecured personal loan (at a higher interest rate) would be a possibility.  The kit it self would cost ?$5000-8000.  Then there is the donor car and all the needed upgrades.  If a bank will loan you the money, they want something to easily sell to recoup the money if you default on the loan.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-04-2001||12:26 PM||||Unless your credit is almost perfect.  If you have outstanding credit and owe very little, with some good credit history (lots of things you've paid on or off), you just might be able to talk your bank into it.  Especially if you've banked at the same place for a few years.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Adrift||11-04-2001||12:44 PM||||The best advice I can give to anyone interesting in purchasing/building a kit is that if you are not in a steady financial situation don't attempt it! It will suck more funds out of you then think, and if you can't support it then it will just become a nice fiberglass statue in the middle of your back yard. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||GTFiero1||11-04-2001||12:46 PM||||remember a lambo kit may be inexpesive as a kit but the costs add up really fast. streching and all that. it would be cheaper to get a kit that requires no frame cutting at all, like archies Fino or Fanale <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>www.v8archie.com</A>   or a ferrari 308 <A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A> <P>------------------<BR>Adam J. B.||||reg||1
